      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Letting go doesn't have to mean giving up—it can mean releasing the pressure to make everything matter. You're allowed to stop running and just sit with the silence, even if it feels empty. But if you're thinking about stepping off in a way that would end your story, that's not logic—that's pain talking, and it deserves gentleness, not obedience. You don't have to find meaning today; you just have to stay here long enough to see if tomorrow feels different.",
